description: The sent short link publishes a draft; the trainer can hide it
alwaysApply: true
---

# Trainer publish

An imported profile stays `draft` until a visitor opens the short link `/hi/{code}` that staff sent. That visit publishes the card. A logged-in staff visit does not. The trainer can hide the page again from the cabinet. A later visit does not publish a hidden or archived card.

Import, a server copy, a password, and a Google sign-in do not publish it. The link visit does. The account window stays on that visit until the card has an owner.

## Do

- Save and sync an imported profile as `draft`.
- Publish the draft when a non-staff visitor opens `/hi/{code}`.
- Keep the account window until the card has an owner, including after that publish.
- Let the trainer set the page to hidden in the cabinet.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: the import publishes, or a hidden card is published again
await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.slug, slug));

// right: only a draft, and only when the sent link is opened by someone who is not staff
if (!staff && row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}
```
